{"name":"Muscadine","hex":"#f4e5ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"muscadine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An American vine of the subgenus Vitis subg. Muscadinia, Vitis rotundifolia","A grape variety from this vine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/muscadine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vitis rotundifolia","blocks":[{"text":"Vitis rotundifolia, or muscadine or swamp grape, is a grapevine species native to the southeastern and south-central United States. The growth range extends from Florida to New Jersey coast, and west to eastern Texas and Oklahoma. It has been extensively cultivated since the 16th century. The plants are well-adapted to their native warm and humid climate; they need fewer chilling hours than better known varieties, and thrive in summer heat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Vitis_rotundifolia.jpg/330px-Vitis_rotundifolia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitis_rotundifolia","wikidata":"Q2701573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/North_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg/500px-North_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/North_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg/1280px-North_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/North_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg/500px-North_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North Carolina muscadine grapes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANorth_Carolina_muscadine_grapes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Muscadines.Scuppernongs.jpg/500px-Muscadines.Scuppernongs